          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "FAQ",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What types of wedding candles can I buy in bulk from Kisco Candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We offer bulk wedding candles in several of the most popular styles, including pillar candles, taper candles, floating candles, and tea lights. That makes it easier to create a complete wedding candle plan with a single coordinated order rather than sourcing each format separately.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which candle style is best for wedding centerpieces?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The best candle style depends on the centerpiece design. Pillar candles work well for fuller arrangements and larger tables, taper candles suit formal tablescapes and head tables, floating candles are ideal for bowls and glass vases, and tea lights add soft accent lighting around florals, signage, and small decorative details.<br/></p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I choose between white and ivory wedding candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>White candles are a strong fit for crisp, bright palettes, while ivory candles work beautifully with warmer florals, cream linens, champagne tones, and more traditional wedding décor. If you want a cohesive look across the ceremony and reception, it usually helps to stay within one color family throughout the order.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_TCpCmP": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I mix candle styles in one wedding order?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zpDMyy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. Many wedding orders combine more than one candle style so each part of the event has the right scale and look. A common approach is to use pillars for statement pieces, tapers for dining tables, floating candles for water-based centerpieces, and tea lights for smaller accent areas.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_TBLF9D": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fYqbBp": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are your bulk wedding candles unscented?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_Tw9Caw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Many customers choose Kisco Candles for wedding use because unscented candles are the safest fit around food, florals, and guest seating. They help create ambiance without adding fragrance that may compete with the meal or the room itself.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_nffgym": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_c3XmjU": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How far in advance should I place a bulk wedding candle order?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_KWgxh6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We recommend placing your order about 2 to 3 weeks before the wedding. That gives you extra time for shipping, mockups, final guest-count changes, and setup planning before the event date.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_anfkh7": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_DxNQtr": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Do you ship wedding candle orders directly to venues or planners?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_7PFV9E": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. We can ship directly to your venue, planner, or event location when the delivery details are entered correctly at checkout. That can simplify logistics, especially for larger weddings with lengthy décor checklists.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_aycWjD": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_rBTBg6": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I estimate how many wedding candles I need?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_aXU3WV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Start with the number of tables, centerpiece designs, and accent areas that need candlelight. Then count ceremony décor, reception tables, welcome displays, bar areas, and any extra styling moments, and add a small buffer so you are not short during setup.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_JYbAfc": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_NXA4rf": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are bulk wedding candles a good option for larger weddings?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_8PE6UY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. Bulk wedding candles are a practical choice for larger guest counts and multi-space events because they help maintain a consistent overall look while making quantity planning easier. They are also useful for planners, venues, and stylists who need repeatable candle setups across several tables or rooms.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_qg8jzH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_AbAQ34": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Do larger wedding candle orders help reduce the cost per candle?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_bEeXdE": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. Buying in bulk is one of the easiest ways to keep the cost per candle lower while still using coordinated products across the event. It is especially helpful when you need the same color story and candle style repeated across many tables.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        }
      },
